[{"sha":"af19328ff85bf9e0f6e938b39e5c859e4ddb091d","node_id":"C_kwDOP9R419oAKGFmMTkzMjhmZjg1YmY5ZTBmNmU5MzhiMzllNWM4NTllNGRkYjA5MWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"David Burke","email":"david@burkesoftware.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:09:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"David Burke","email":"david@burkesoftware.com","date":"2026-06-02T19:14:54Z"},"message":"Assign self.connection before set_isolation_level await\n\nWhen `isolation_level` is set in OPTIONS, get_new_connection()\nawaits set_isolation_level() *after* checking a connection out of\nthe pool but before any caller code can record the handle on the\nwrapper. If cancellation lands inside that await, the conn stays\nin the pool's in-use accounting but no reference exists on the\nwrapper, so close()/middleware can't putconn() it -- the slot is\nstranded for the life of the pool.\n\nAssigning self.connection before the set_isolation_level await\nfixes this: close()'s usual putconn() path now reaches the\nchecked-out conn even if cancellation interrupts the await.\n\nThe added test installs a barrier in psycopg's set_isolation_level,\ncancels the connect task while parked, calls close() (the ASGI\nmiddleware's job), and verifies the pool's full capacity is still\nacquireable. Without the fix the second getconn() blocks on the\npool's timeout; with it both probes succeed.","tree":{"sha":"6efd822af2af02cbbe593a016c7d7cbc2e389e82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arfey/django-async-backend/git/trees/6efd822af2af02cbbe593a016c7d7cbc2e389e82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arfey/django-async-backend/git/commits/af19328ff85bf9e0f6e938b39e5c859e4ddb091d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arfey/django-async-backend/commits/af19328ff85bf9e0f6e938b39e5c859e4ddb091d","html_url":"https://github.com/Arfey/django-async-backend/commit/af19328ff85bf9e0f6e938b39e5c859e4ddb091d","comments_url":"https://api.g